<h3>Capability & Qualifications</h3><br />

<ul>
	<li><b><u>Financial Sustainability</u></b> <br/> As a non-profit organization, our management structure includes our Board of Directors as the overarching managing entity of the corporation. All members of the Board of Directors are non-compensated for their 
		service to the organization. Board members are not agents or staff members of the corporation. Membership consists of representatives from the community and primary service agencies including County Government, 
		The City of Fayetteville, The CC Sheriff’s Office, Fayetteville Police Department, CC Schools, State government, Business Leaders and Community Advocates. CommuniCare is <b>fully compliant with all respective laws 
		and tax codes</b>. A 990 has been submitted annually in accordance with such regulations. CommuniCare is current on all local, state and federal tax filings and payments. Our corporation has no overdue tax debt or 
		any other kind of debt. No tax liabilities or liens have been leveraged against the corporation at any time in our history. CommuniCare has never been sanctioned by any funder and not lost funding to poor 
		performance or mismanagement of resources. Evidence of the corporation’s previous success relative to these strategic directions is documented by our procurement of contracts and grants from local, state and 
		federal sources including private foundations. By winning these contracts and grant awards, as well as earning a place under the United Way of Cumberland County family of member agencies, CommuniCare, Inc. 
		now distinguishes itself as an organization that has the technical and operational capabilities to provide services as outlined in the strategic fashion noted, at high levels of technical competence.
	</li>
</ul>

<ul>
	<li><b><u>Service Philosophy</u></b> <br/> The overarching philosophy is that no one is turned away from services for an inability to pay. When the consumer’s needs rest in another program type or service, such as intellectual developmental disabilities, 
		CommuniCare staff takes time to assist the consumer in reaching an appropriate provider including directions, phone numbers, etc. and at times, we may assist the consumer in making a call to schedule an appointment. 
		It is an important part of our work in the community to assist consumers that need our help in navigating this complex system. CommuniCare utilizes the System of Care model because of the inclusion of natural supports, 
		consumers, families, schools, courts, area service providers and others from across domains that are important to the treatment and recovery of the consumer. Our services are consumer focused and family driven. 
		All consumers are involved in a Child & Family team (CFT) or Treatment Team meeting to discuss assessment results and treatment recommendations. All consumers receive information about area providers and resources 
		and given provider choice at every level of service even though our agency provides most of the primary services.  When medical needs are identified on the comprehensive clinical assessment (CCA) and/or during the 
		CFT/Treatment team, coordination is sought to secure a follow-up to address the presenting problem(s).  When a consumer does not identify a primary health care provider and does not have insurance they are referred 
		to the Public Health Department for services. Our treatment philosophy is centered in the System of Care model. CommuniCare provides comprehensive, wrap-around supports for every consumer and family served in our 
		agency. The RF model expanded our use of objective, empirically supported screening tools to use findings to systematically link all youth processed at intake, referred to the court for further action and those 
		placed on juvenile court supervision and their families to appropriate levels of intervention in our local system of care. 
	</li>
</ul>

